From: Shigeaki Asai <ShigeakiAsai@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: clk: samsung: exynos-audss: defer probe until pll_in
 is available

The "pll_in" clock is optional, so a failed devm_clk_get() is silently
ignored and mout_audss is registered with pll_ref as its only parent.

On Exynos5420/5800 "pll_in" is CLK_MAU_EPLL, a gate clock of the MAU
sub-CMU. When the sub-CMU registration is deferred until the power
domains are available, this clock is not registered yet when the audss
clock controller probes. Audio then runs from the 24 MHz pll_ref and
48 kHz playback is about twice as fast as it should be
("failed to reparent mout_audss to mau_epll: -22").

Defer the probe when "pll_in" returns -EPROBE_DEFER.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos-audss.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos-audss.c
@@ -153,6 +153,9 @@
 
 	pll_ref = devm_clk_get(dev, "pll_ref");
 	pll_in = devm_clk_get(dev, "pll_in");
+	if (pll_in == ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER))
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -EPROBE_DEFER,
+				     "pll_in clock not ready\n");
 	if (!IS_ERR(pll_ref))
 		mout_audss_p[0] = __clk_get_name(pll_ref);
 	if (!IS_ERR(pll_in)) {
